{"availability":"available","full":"NuclearTalent/MachineLearningECT2021","name":"MachineLearningECT2021","description":"Display of daily teaching material as jupyter-book at https://compphysics.github.io/MachineLearning/doc/LectureNotes/_build/html/intro.html","category":"Education","language":null,"stars":9,"forks":5,"created":"2021-05-07T01:42:47Z","updated":"2023-05-04T17:55:16Z","license":"CC0-1.0","branch":"gh-pages","homepage":"https://nucleartalent.github.io/MachineLearningECT2021/doc/web/course.html","topics":[],"demo":"https://nucleartalent.github.io/MachineLearningECT2021/doc/web/course.html","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.514Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.514Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.514Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.514Z","stars":9,"forks":5}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Machine Learning and Data Analysis for Nuclear Physics, a Nuclear TALENT Course at the ECT, Trento, Italy, July 19 to July 30 2021.","Probability theory and statistical methods play a central role in science. Nowadays we are surrounded by huge amounts of data. For example, there are about one trillion web pages; more than one hour of video is uploaded to YouTube every second, amounting to 10 years of content every day; the genomes of 1000s of people, each of which has a length of more than a billion base pairs, have been sequenced by various labs and so on. This deluge of data calls for automated methods of data analysis, which is exactly what machine learning provides. The purpose of this Nuclear Talent course is to…","The goals of the Nuclear Talent course on Machine Learning and Data Analysis are to give the participants a deeper understanding and critical view of several widely popular Machine Learning algorithms, covering both supervised and unsupervised learning. The learning outcomes involve an understanding of the following central methods:"],"features":["Basic concepts of machine learning and data analysis and statistical concepts like expectation values, variance, covariance, correlation functions and errors;","Estimation of errors using cross-validation, blocking, bootstrapping and jackknife methods;","Optimization of functions","Linear Regression and Logistic Regression;","Dimensionality reductions, from PCA to clustering"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuclearTalent/MachineLearningECT2021/blob/gh-pages/README.md","fingerprint":"b191bba299cf6a3115b8502969b556670d0a68536e54a0544046f2aaf99b1f9d","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.625Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.625Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Machine Learning and Data Analysis for Nuclear Physics, a Nuclear TALENT Course at the ECT, Trento, Italy, July 19 to July 30 2021.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuclearTalent/MachineLearningECT2021/blob/gh-pages/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"If you login to your University Library or access this site via a University IP number, you can download for free the textbook in PDF format or epub format.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuclearTalent/MachineLearningECT2021/blob/gh-pages/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"b191bba299cf6a3115b8502969b556670d0a68536e54a0544046f2aaf99b1f9d","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuclearTalent/MachineLearningECT2021/blob/gh-pages/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.625Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-05-04T17:55:16Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/NuclearTalent/MachineLearningECT2021/blob/gh-pages/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T05:01:30.627Z","hash":"b191bba299cf6a3115b8502969b556670d0a68536e54a0544046f2aaf99b1f9d","originalBytes":13546,"storedBytes":13546,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["learning","nuclear","data","machine","course","cet","analysis","methods","students","physics","pm-4pm","statistical","networks","neural","slides","theory","unde